# Platform UI governance

Applies to **all product work** (app routes, shells, features). The design system site (`app/(platform)/bdn/designsystem/`) has **separate layout rules** and must **not** use `PageCanvas`.

## Locales

- No user-facing English inline in `app/`, `components/`, or `lib/`.
- Add copy under `locales/{locale}.json` (product) or `locales/bdn/{locale}.json` (design system). See [contracts/i18n-locales.md](../../contracts/i18n-locales.md). Wire with `t("…")` from `@/lib/i18n`.
- Exception: `app/(platform)/bdn/designsystem/ui/**` showcase demos only (ESLint ignore).

## Icons

- Never import `lucide-react` outside `components/ui/icons/`.
- **Product pages and shells:** use the `Icon` atom (`name` from registry), not `@/components/ui/icons/*Icon` directly.
- **Design system routes** (`app/(platform)/bdn/designsystem/**`): registry imports allowed for docs/showcases; prefer `Icon` atom for new code.

## Tokens

- Color/spacing/type values live in `tokens/*.css`; utilities wired in `tailwind.config.mjs` / `tokens/tailwind-theme-extend.mjs`.
- No hex/rgb/hsl literals in `className`. No legacy palette classes (`bg-pink-*`, `text-navy-*`, etc.).
- No arbitrary Tailwind brackets for layout (`max-w-[1440px]`, `min-h-[calc(...)]`) — use layout tokens (`max-w-content`, `min-h-main-below-header`, etc.) or flag a token extension.

## No ad-hoc UI on screens

- Pages and route layouts **compose** existing atoms → molecules → composites from `components/ui/`.
- Do not ship one-off buttons, fields, nav rows, or styled primitives in `app/**` when the design system already has (or should have) a component.
- If a piece is missing: **stop**, flag an atomic design extension, do not improvise.

## Layout shells

- **`LayoutShell`** (`components/layout/`) — global structure only (header + main slot). No page meaning.
- **`PageCanvas`** — future app page layout enforcement; no structure/chrome. **Not used under `app/(platform)/bdn/designsystem/`.**
- **Design system** — owns padding/max-width in `app/(platform)/bdn/designsystem/layout.tsx` and nested layouts.

## When rules conflict with a mockup

Flag the conflict; propose the correct atom/molecule/composite or missing token. Do not implement the anti-pattern to match the ask.
